  "answer_text": "In Massachusetts, the maximum amount you can collect for unemployment depends on whether you have dependents, how much you previously earned, and how many weeks you are eligible to receive benefits. \n\nThe maximum caps and durations are outlined below:\n\n### 1. Maximum Weekly Benefit Amount (Base)\n* **Maximum Base Benefit:** **$1,105 per week**\n* *Note:* This maximum rate went into effect on October 5, 2025, and remains active. The state recalculates and typically updates this cap annually in early October. Your actual base benefit will equal roughly **50% of your average weekly wage** during your highest-earning quarters, up to this $1,105 cap.\n\n### 2. Dependency Allowance (Extra Weekly Benefits)\nIf you are the main source of financial support for dependent children, you may qualify for an additional allowance:\n* **Allowance Amount:** **$25 per week per child**.\n* **Qualifications:** Dependents must be under 18, under 24 if they are a full-time student, or any age if they are unable to work due to a physical or mental disability.\n* **The Cap:** The total dependency allowance **cannot exceed 50% of your base weekly benefit**. (For someone receiving the maximum base rate of $1,105, the theoretical maximum dependency cap is $552.50 per week, though this would require having 22 qualifying dependents). \n\n### 3. Maximum Benefit Duration\n* **Maximum Weeks:** **Up to 30 weeks**.\n* *Note:* While the standard maximum duration in Massachusetts is often 26 weeks, state law triggers a 30-week maximum extension when regional unemployment rates rise above a certain threshold (a trigger that remains active).\n\n### 4. Maximum Total Payout\n* **Without Dependents:** If you qualify for the maximum base benefit for the full 30 weeks, the most you can collect in a benefit year is **$33,150** ($1,105 \u00d7 30 weeks).\n* **With Dependents:** If you qualify for the maximum base benefit and have, for example, 3 dependent children, you would receive $1,180 per week ($1,105 base + $75 dependency allowance). Over 30 weeks, your maximum total payout would be **$35,400**.",
